<title>JAPAN: Asahi Bank says almost overcomes bad loan problem.</title>
<headline>Asahi Bank says almost overcomes bad loan problem.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asahi Bank Ltd said on Tuesday it had almost overcome its problem loans by writing off bad debts worth 400 billion yen in the year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>A bank spokesman said it believes it will be able to cover remaining bad debts from the 1997/98 business year onward using revenues from its core banking business.</p>
<p>The bad debts of 400 billion yen written off in 1996/97 included 270 billion yen in loans to its non-bank affiliates, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>He did not elaborate further.</p>
</text>
